{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/112352-any-ice-freezing-abilities-in-cwod","id":112352,"title":"Any Ice/Freezing Abilities in CWOD?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-13T17:59:18-07:00","id":112352,"title":"Any Ice/Freezing Abilities in CWOD?","content":"I've been trying to see if any of the game lines have a power set that can allow a character to either conjure ice or freeze people, but so far I've found nothing. The reason I'm asking is I'm trying to create ether a vampire or mage who can turn people's body parts into ice and then shatter them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2256-goblin404","name":"Goblin404","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2256_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T18:18:05-07:00","id":112356,"title":"","content":"I don't know about Sorcery or Tremere magic but Sphere Magic* could. If you're asking about specific spells there's none at the top of my head.<br /> <br /> *Primarily Forces as it's the Sphere that deals with the Elements. Though you'd need some Prime too if you wished to conjure ice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T18:53:35-07:00","id":112366,"title":"","content":"Changelings had Kryos, which was a freezing art, and the Shifters had numerous icey Gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T19:42:04-07:00","id":112387,"title":"","content":"Read the Wendigo Gifts. A great example is their level 5 that freezes the heart. But they especially have many.<br /> A Mage can do whatever you want, so long as it is fluffed. I would say to do what you say would require Forces 2 + Life 3.<br /> For vamps, I don't know. Maybe use some of the spirit-based thau to summon ice spirits?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i>&quot;Maturity is knowing you were an idiot in the past.&quot;<br /> &quot;If that's true, then Wisdom is knowing you'll be an idiot in the future.&quot;<br /> &quot;And Common Sense is knowing that you should try not to be an idiot NOW.&quot;<br /> -Questionable Content 976</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1042-zhyzhaksmate","name":"ZhyzhaksMate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1042_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T21:35:30-07:00","id":112411,"title":"","content":"Mage ice effects would generally fall under Matter. Though you'd need some other Spheres for certain effects as usual for the game.<br /> <br /> Forces + Life could lower body temperature to freezing, causing hypothermia, but you'd want Matter + Life to instantly turn someone into ice (or any other suitably brittle material).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T02:31:34-07:00","id":112499,"title":"","content":"Tremere could easily create a sort of Glacial Way, following the base line on Blood Magic","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T04:50:53-07:00","id":112543,"title":"","content":"Sorcerers have the path of Hellfire in Sorcerer revised, is has a sleet effect but also it gives a good template for creating your own freezing art. I used this a long time ago to create &quot;Sub-Zero&quot; effects like those shown in the Mortal Kombat games and movies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T12:08:42-07:00","id":112842,"title":"","content":"Ice and snow effects would be very thematic for Tzimisce Koldunism (published in V20 core, and the Players' Guide to the High Clans). The Way of Wind 2 offer a slow freeze effect that could freeze a limb over several rounds. For a 2nd dot power, that's pretty impressive.<br /> <br /> If you want a purer &quot;ice mage&quot; schtick in Vampire, I'd talk to your ST about making a custom Path/Way to do it. Template it on an existing direct-damage Path, using most of the system and changing the cosmetic effects.<br /> <br /> Hermetic Path of Winter's Bite (Tremere style):<br /> Start with the Lure of Flames rules. Instead of making fire, you make ice crystals. Rather than the Palm of Flame effect, you may summon a small chunk of ice within your hands. More successes on the activation roll allow for more complex shape. 1 success yields a rough, irregular ice crystal. 5 success will allow you to summon a miniature ice sculpture in the shape you desire.<br /> <br /> When you use the &quot;place flame where you want it&quot; side of things, you are inflicting a deep freeze in that area instead. Frostbite inflicts damage to living and unliving tissue just as fire consumes it. Inanimate objects are similarily damaged by freezing or moisture, though this is often less destructive than fire. Surfaces become slick, dangerously so at high levels of the Path.<br /> <br /> Koldunic Way of Ice (Tzimisce style):<br /> Based on Way of Fire. Use its system for rolls and damage/magnitude.<br /> \u2022 Frozen Resolve<br /> Gain soak dice against ice and cold effects equal to your rating in Way of Ice.<br /> -or-<br /> Borrow the first dot power from Way of Wind or Way of Earth. Either one can be given an icy theme and make sense.<br /> Grasping Soil becomes Winter's Shackles and has ice crystals growing and snaking up the victim's legs instead of dirt.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022 Freeze<br /> Direct damage freezing effect. Just change it costmetically. The target partially freezes.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Blizzard Pallisade<br /> Functionally like Wall of Magma, but the barrier consists of a highly localize storm of roiling snow and ice.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Cold Snap<br /> Functionally like Heat Wave. All moisture is drawn out from the victim, swirling into a cloud of tiny crystals that dance around them until both cloud and victim collapse.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Freezing Geyser<br /> Functionally like Volcanic Blast, except that solid rock isn't left behind (it just doesn't make sense). Geysers of fast moving, freezing cold water erupt from the earth and any other pipe, chasm or body of water in the vicinity. Like freezing rain, this gush freezes upon contact with anything, encasing the affected area in an icy prison and inflicting severe frostbite upon any living or unliving things touched by it. <br /> <br /> The cold is severe enough that the ice remains at least for the rest of the night, trapping everything within it, no matter how warm the weather might otherwise be. In cold winter climates, the ice can remain until the natural spring thaw.<br /> <br /> <br /> Your ST can set a threshold for how much aggravated damage from either of these powers would count as limb-shattering. I'd go with two for an arm, three for a leg, but he/she may feel differently. I just made these up on the spot, so they probably could benefit from refinement before play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Demon Cat</b></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://flamingporcupine.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Illuminated Dark Ages character sheets and more</a>","edited":{"userid":10,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10-demon-cat","user":"Demon Cat","date":". 04-14-2014, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10-demon-cat","name":"Demon Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"266"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T02:27:56-07:00","id":116866,"title":"","content":"Per others responses, as well: yeah -- a mage could create cold effects very easily, so long as their Sphere-emphasis provided for that. Forces:2 could freeze simple objects/things pre-disposed to being frozen (by controlling the heat in, say, a given body of water to be directed elsewhere); Forces:3 could more readily freeze most things in general by transforming any active heat into its metaphysical opposite (freezing people, etc.,); Matter:2 coupled with Forces:3 would allow you to manifest ice from practically thin air by transforming ambient air/moisture into water and then freezing it (if you wanted to create massive amounts -- relative to the environment you're in -- of ice, then you'd have to transform local rock/whatnot into ice with the above, or add Prime:2 to it to create such from literally nothing). <br /> <br /> I'm surprised you (the OP) have said you were wanting to make a vampire or a mage but haven't &quot;found anything&quot; about creating ice-effects: that sort of thing is clearly indicated in Mage via the listed spheres/effects. (Of course, in Dark Ages: Mage, things are even conceptually simpler, as the general concept of a given thing can be included in a given Pillar, as is the case with ice/freezing things, which can be easily accomplished with, for example, Vires:3 for a Hermetic mage, Winter:3 for an Old Faith/pagan witch, or Hjalder:3 for a Valdaerman/Norseman; the other Fellowships can similarly create such effects by adding a lesser level to a comparative base Pillar to effect such, like with The Messianics using Rapha-El:2, Uri-El:2/3 to manifest simple or slightly more complex cold/ice, etc...). Just saying...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T12:13:02-07:00","id":130058,"title":"","content":"I imagine that a Mage could also use Spirit to summon spirits of ice, winter, and wind, and get them to freeze stuff. Some Wendigo Gifts actually do specifically that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T12:22:25-07:00","id":130070,"title":"","content":"In Dark Ages Fae, there is the Dominion of Night which allows for a variety of cold based powers, as it represents the powers of winter fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T04:10:06-07:00","id":136514,"title":"","content":"The weird koldunic path in Clanbook Tzimisce had some Icy wind powers, could copy their systems, it was mostly about halving people's movement rates and affecting dicepools if I'm not mistaken... The path itself wasn't particularly good though and the powers a bit over the top but the idea for the ice power mechanics was nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>former lightmaguz","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/514-auron","name":"Auron","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T07:54:19-07:00","id":136702,"title":"","content":"In regards to Mage, there are a million ways to do this. It depends on your paradigm. <br /> <br /> Forces could control the heat of an object, removing it would cause things to get very cold and freeze.<br /> Matter could actually control ice itself, but would have difficulty affecting the environment without a major working.<br /> Entropy and/or Time could make already existing ice stronger or weaker, take it further or closer to the melting point. (sort of an obtuse solution)<br /> <br /> So if I was creating a full-fledged Ice-Only type mage, the best way to get him going would be Forces 3, Matter 3, Prime 2. I can't imagine much ice-related you couldn't do with that alone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}